From: Package maintainers <packages@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] bluetoothd: search layered system configuration paths
Source: https://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/bluetooth/bluez-5.85.tar.xz
Upstream: Not submitted; this is a generic UAPI configuration proposal.

Keep an explicit --configfile path exact. When a service manager supplies
CONFIGURATION_DIRECTORY, search every directory in its declared order first,
then continue through the administrator, transient, and vendor trees. Select
the first existing configuration file.

Use the same selector for main.conf, both input.conf readers, and
network.conf. An existing empty file therefore masks lower policy.

Fall back past CONFIGURATION_DIRECTORY. The installed bluetooth.service sets
ConfigurationDirectory=bluetooth, so a service manager exports that variable
as the administrator directory alone. Searching only that list made the
package default under /usr/lib/bluetooth unreachable on every normal service
start. Search the exported directories first, then continue through the
administrator, transient, and vendor trees.

